# RealChord feature showcase – every ChordPro feature supported by the app.
# All lyrics and music in this file are original and free to use.
# Import it (or feature-showcase.zip, which also contains the image) via
# Songs → Import files. The {new_song} at the end creates a second song.

{title: Feature Showcase}
{sorttitle: Showcase, Feature}
{subtitle: Every directive in one song}
{artist: The RealChord Band}
{sortartist: RealChord Band, The}
{composer: A. Composer}
{composer: B. Composer}
{lyricist: C. Lyricist}
{arranger: D. Arranger}
{copyright: 2026 RealChord (free to use)}
{album: Test Recordings}
{year: 2026}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 96}
{duration: 3:45}
{capo: 0}
{tag: Test}
{tag: Showcase}
{meta: mood happy}
{meta: duet true}
# RealChord custom directive (x_ prefix, ignored by other ChordPro tools):
# song sequence, shown below the subtitle
# (C=Chorus, V=Verse, PC=Pre-chorus, B=Bridge, I=Intro, O=Outro, …).
{x_sequence: I, V1, C, V2, PC, C x2, B, O}
{x_realchord_note: custom directives starting with x_ are ignored}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Metadata in texts and comment styles
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
{comment: %{title} by %{artist} – key %{key}, %{tempo} BPM}
{comment: Composers: %{composer} (first: %{composer.1}, last: %{composer.-1})}
{comment_italic: %{album|Album: %{}|No album} · %{year=2026|This year|Another year}}
{comment_box: Instrument: %{instrument|%{}|not set} · User: %{user|%{}|not set}}
{highlight: Highlighted comment}
{c: Escaped markup characters: \%\{not metadata\}}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sections, labels, markup and chords
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
{start_of_verse: label="Verse 1\nAll voices"}
[G]Markup in lyrics: <b>bold</b>, <i>italic</i>, <u>underlined</u>, <s>struck</s>,
[Em]<span color="red">red</span>, <span size="larger">larger</span>, <sup>sup</sup> and <sub>sub</sub>,
[C]<tt>monospace</tt>, <span background="#fff59d">highlighted</span> and [D]<b>bold [G]across</b> chords.
[G]Chords with markup: [<b>Am</b>]bold chord, [*<i>Rit.</i>]annotation, [N.C.]no chord.
[G]Optional chords: [(D/F#)]in parentheses, [Cadd9]extensions, [Dsus4]suspended, [G7(b9)]altered.
[G]German and Dutch names: [Hm]H minor, [Fis]Fis, [Bes]Bes, [Es]Es, [As]As.
[G]Chord spellings: [Ami7]Ami7, [A-7]A-7, [CΔ7]CΔ7, [Bø]Bø, [C°7]C°7.
[G]Escaped brackets: \[not a chord\] and an inline chord [C]here.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C]This is the [G]chorus, it [D]stands out
[C]with a bar on the [D]left side, [G]no doubt.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[Em]A bridge without a label uses the [C]default label,
[Am]chords above the [D]words, as stable as a table.
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_outro}
[G]A custom section (start_of_outro) is shown as lyrics.
{end_of_outro}

{chorus}
{chorus: Chorus (again, with a label)}

# Section headings as comments (as in CCLI SongSelect files):
{comment: Chorus 2}
[C]A comment heading [G]becomes a chorus section.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transposition, key changes and Nashville numbers
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
{start_of_verse: Transposition}
[C]No transposition: [D]D [E]E [F]F
{transpose: 2}
[C]{transpose: 2} (sharps): [D]D [E]E [F]F
{transpose: -10}
[C]{transpose: -10} (flats): [D]D [E]E [F]F
{transpose: 2f}
[C]{transpose: 2f} (flats forced): [D]D [E]E [F]F
{transpose}
{transpose}
{transpose}
[C]Back to no transposition: [D]D [E]E [F]F
{end_of_verse}

{key: A}
{start_of_verse: Modulation to A}
[A]After {key: A} Nashville [D]numbers [E]follow the new key.
{end_of_verse}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tab and grid
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
{start_of_tab: Riff}
e|-----0---0-----|
B|---1---1---1---|
G|-2-----------2-|
{end_of_tab}

{start_of_grid shape="1+4x2+4" label="Intro grid"}
A    || G7 . | % . | %% . | . . |
     | C7 . | %  . || G7 . | % . ||
     |: C7 . | %  . :|: G7~D7 . | / . :| repeat 4 times
Coda | D7 . | Eb7 . |1 D7 . |2 G7 . |.
{end_of_grid}

{start_of_grid label="Strums"}
| S dn up dn up |
| s d u ux x |
{end_of_grid}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fonts, sizes and colours
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
{start_of_verse: Formats}
Normal text line.
{textfont: serif}
{textsize: 120%}
{textcolour: #1e88e5}
Serif, 120 %, blue text.
{chordcolour: red}
{chordsize: 14}
[G]Red chords at 14 pt [C]size.
{textfont: monospace 12}
Monospace 12 pt.
# A directive without value restores the previous value (a stack):
{textfont}
Serif again (previous font restored).
{textfont}
{textsize}
{textcolour}
{chordcolour}
{chordsize}
[G]Back to normal [C]formats.
{labelcolour: green}
{end_of_verse}

{choruscolour: #43a047}
{start_of_chorus: Green chorus}
[C]Chorus lyrics are [G]green.
{end_of_chorus}
{choruscolour}
{labelcolour}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Conditional directives (Settings → My instrument / My name or voice)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
{comment-guitar: Shown only for guitar}
{comment-ukulele: Shown only for ukulele}
{comment-keyboard: Shown only for keyboard}
{comment-guitar!: Shown for every instrument except guitar}
{comment-alto: Shown only for the user "alto"}
{comment-duet: Shown because the meta item "duet" is true}
{comment-nosuchmeta: Never shown}
{start_of_verse-soprano: Soprano only}
[C]This whole section is only shown for the user "soprano".
{end_of_verse}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Chord diagrams (Settings → Chord diagrams, or {diagrams})
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
{define: Am base-fret 1 frets x 0 2 2 1 0 fingers 0 0 2 3 1 0}
{define: G6 base-fret 1 frets 3 2 0 0 0 0}
{define-ukulele: G6 base-fret 1 frets 0 2 0 2}
{define: Hm7 copy Bm7 display B minor 7}
{define: Csus2 diagram off}
{diagrams: bottom}
{start_of_verse: Diagrams}
[Am]Defined Am, [G6]defined G6, [Csus2]no diagram for Csus2.
{chord: Am}
{chord: E7 base-fret 1 frets 0 2 0 1 0 0}
{chord: [Dm]}
{end_of_verse}

